# Build-time configuration, committed on purpose — see .gitignore for why this one file is exempt
# from the .env* rule. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle by `next build` and
# are therefore public by construction; never put a secret here.

# Turns on the live WebSocket connection used by chat delivery, typing indicators, and Office
# presence. Off by default (lib/collab/collabWsUrl.ts) as a deliberate manual gate: the Hocuspocus
# sidecar listens on plain ws:// port 1234, which has no TLS in front of it, so it is only usable
# in production via the same-origin `/collab` proxy in server/customServer.ts. That proxy is
# deployed and working, so this is now on.
#
# Read at BUILD time, not at runtime: changing it requires a Pterodactyl *Reinstall* (which
# rebuilds), not a Restart. A restart alone will appear to do nothing.
#
# With this off, chat falls back to a 6s poll while a conversation is open
# (lib/collab/useChatChannelConnection.ts) — messages still arrive, just not instantly, and typing
# indicators do not work at all. Set it back to false if the socket ever misbehaves; the fallback
# takes over automatically.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COLLAB_WS_ENABLED=true
